{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, sorry the VPN is giving you trouble in Lisbon. I checked your side and everything looks fine: your account is active, VPN access is on, Duo is set up, and your VPN connected from Lisbon earlier today. None of your attempts since then have reached our VPN server, so the hotel Wi-Fi is probably blocking the connection before it gets to us. Please try these steps in order: 1) Make sure you have internet without the VPN by opening any public website. 2) Open a browser and go to a plain site like example.com. If the hotel's Wi-Fi sign-in or 'accept terms' page appears, accept it, and enter your room details if asked. 3) Quit the VPN client completely, reopen it, and connect. Approve the Duo push on your phone. If the push doesn't arrive, open Duo Mobile and pull down to refresh. 4) If it still fails, restart your laptop and try again. 5) If the hotel Wi-Fi still won't work, try your phone's hotspot. That will tell us whether the hotel network is the problem. If none of this works, reply with the exact error the VPN shows and whether the hotspot worked, and we'll take it from there. Also, your laptop is almost out of disk space (about 9 GB free), so it's worth deleting large files you don't need when you have a minute. Good luck with the presentation!",
  "internal_note": "KB-013 checks: account active, sign_in_blocked=false, vpn_access=true, failed_login_count=0. Duo push enrolled. Sign-in logs: daily VPN successes from Lisbon, PT (198.51.100.66, Duo push), the latest at 2026-10-09 08:05 UTC. There are no failed_password or mfa_denied entries and no failed attempts at all after that. This matches a trip that started from NY on 10/05. The failing attempts aren't reaching the server, which points to the hotel network or captive portal blocking it, or the client. KB-013 escalation criteria are not met. Laptop BL-LT-0106 is online (checked in 14:51 UTC) but has low disk space, 3.5% free. Sent the captive-portal, client restart, reboot, and hotspot steps. If the user comes back saying it still fails on the hotspot and attempts still don't show up in the logs, escalate to Tier 2 with the client error.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-016"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
